Hi,
    Sorry if this is a newbie question.  I'm using ezPLOT to plot the
results of a repeated measures ANOVA (done with ezANOVA).  Everything
works like a charm, but I'd like to change the colours of the error
bars.  The default is for the two levels of my experiment (determined
for the plot by the "split" command) to be green and pink (or
something close to those colours).  They don't stand out very well
against the background, so I was hoping to change them to something
more salient, like red and blue.  Is there a way to do this?
    Any ideas would be very welcome,
    Thanks!
    Mark

